     "answer": "1) The vet knew at once that there was nothing really wrong with Tricki's body; the dog was sick because of overfeeding and lack of exercise. 2) He also knew that Mrs Pumphrey would never agree to diet her darling, and would go on pampering him at home, so the only way to control the food was to take the dog to his surgery. 3) He therefore told her gravely that Tricki must be hospitalised immediately without delay, and the shocked lady, though she almost swooned at parting, consented. 4) Thus the removal itself was the first half of the treatment, for away from her tender care the dog could be kept hungry and active as his nature demanded."
