     "answer": "1) Mrs Pumphrey believed that her darling was gravely ill in hospital and needed building up, so she sent eggs to be given at breakfast, wine at lunch and brandy at night. 2) The parcels reveal her genuine love, her wealth and her habit of expressing affection through luxuries, since she imagined that delicacies could cure where dieting was actually at work. 3) They also reveal her folly and her ignorance of a dog's needs, for Tricki wanted plain food and exercise, not rich drinks. 4) The comic result is that the vet and his partners consumed the whole supply themselves, and the story gently laughs at loving owners who mistake luxury for care."
